  "chitchat": [
    "The prospector hacks a wet cough into his scarf and keeps raking.",
    "\"One good seam. That's all a man needs. One good seam.\"",
    "\"You hear that ticking? Course you don't. You get used to it.\""
  ],
  "description": "A lean, coughing man who works the scrap mesa with a bent rake and a rad-band he stopped looking at weeks ago. He is convinced the seam he's found will make him rich, and he is running out of the time it would take to spend it.",
  "dialogue_tree": {
    "bye": {
      "options": [],
      "text": "He is already raking again, ticking softly to himself."
    },
    "root": {
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "Good luck with the seam.",
          "next": "bye"
        }
      ],
      "text": "The prospector barely looks up from his rake. \"Claim's mine, if that's what you're wondering. Whole mesa's mine. Found the seam, didn't I. You want a piece, you dig your own — plenty of mesa, plenty of...\" he coughs, \"...plenty of time.\""
    }
  },
